## Context

PR #250 (Phase 2 ablation) shows that replicates of the same prompt
variant receive wildly different token counts: ~72K (no RAG documents)
vs ~350K (RAG documents injected). The two replicates are supposed to
be identical except for random seed.

Evidence from measurements.jsonl:
- DeepSeek p2_sourcing run1: 72,516 tokens (t=null, ok)
- DeepSeek p2_sourcing run2: 353,691 tokens (t=0.0, refusal)
- Kimi p2_composite run1: 282,248 tokens (over-context, ok)
- Kimi p2_composite run2: 75,911 tokens (normal)

Temperature also varies across replicates (null vs 0.0), suggesting
runs straddled the ticket 0084 enforcement boundary.

## Actions

1. Read the worker dispatch code (src/aedist/worker.py, query scripts)
   to trace how RAG documents are loaded and injected into prompts.
2. Check whether RAG injection depends on a flag that changed between
   the two run batches (e.g., a config reload after PR #244 merge).
3. Determine whether the non-determinism is a race condition, a config
   boundary, or an intentional fallback when documents are unavailable.
4. Document the root cause.

## Test

Reproduce: run the same sweep config twice and verify both replicates
get identical token counts (within tokenizer variance).

## Exit criteria

- Root cause identified and documented in ticket log
- Fix proposed (may be a separate ticket if non-trivial)
